      "writtenOn": "2025-01-13T15:41:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, `IOMMU_CACHE` is driven by `dma-coherent` (were this information is not available at EL2, I was thinking about adding flags to attach to pass such per-device information)\n\nBut, my vague memory was we rely on TCU cohereny to check if device traffic is coherent from as `dma-coherent` was not sufficent in that case (maybe something to do with snooping, I can dig more on the list for that)\nhttps://elixir.bootlin.com/linux/v6.12.6/source/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu-v3/arm-smmu-v3.c#L2294",
